nodecode-cloudflare-workers-ai is a rewrite of AhmetArif0's AhmetArif0/hermes-cloudflare-workers-ai-provider:

  https://github.com/AhmetArif0/hermes-cloudflare-workers-ai-provider
  commit f6821d058d504ee6324b0d3217564b93124c09f9
  MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 AhmetArif0 (LICENSE)

Rewritten: the model table of 2026-09-29 (the 16 Workers AI models with
function calling and at least 64K of context, with Cloudflare's context
windows, vision and reasoning flags and the reasoning_effort values each
takes), the reasoning-effort rule (a rung the model does not take becomes the
nearest weaker one, below its lowest becomes that lowest, off becomes `none`
where it is taken), and the account-shaped base URL with the plugin's token
variable. The code itself is a reimplementation against Nodecode's provider
seams, in Common Lisp: Hermes' ProviderProfile with its register_provider call
becomes the cell's catalog row, credential, listing and request-body hooks,
and the model list is data in provider.lisp.

Left out: the free-plan 403 classification (`model_entitlement`, not
retryable, fall back), because Nodecode has no per-provider error classifier
a cell can hook; the picker's `(paid plan)` marker stands in for it. The
plugin's provider id `workers-ai` becomes `cloudflare-workers-ai`, the id
Nodecode's privacy list already carries for the endpoint.
